# json-glib -- JSON parsing with GObject types.
#
# A hard dependency of THREE things in the flatpak plan, which is why it is
# early: flatpak itself (dependency('json-glib-1.0'), no option guard),
# gnome-software (>= 1.6.0), and xdg-desktop-portal if that is ever packaged.
# Its own dependency list is one line -- gio-2.0 -- so it is the cheapest of the
# chain to land.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/json-glib/1.10/json-glib-1.10.6.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=77f4bcbf9339528f166b8073458693f0a20b77b7059dbc2db61746a1928b0293
SRC_DIR=json-glib-1.10.6

# Every option below carries its upstream default, because an option left at
# 'auto' is indistinguishable in a recipe from an option nobody considered, and
# writing the default down is the only evidence a decision happened.
#
# -Dinstalled_tests=false. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE, and this is the one that
# would actually have shipped something wrong: installed_tests INSTALLS TEST
# BINARIES INTO THE PACKAGE. Not a build-time cost -- a payload the package
# would carry to every system that installs it.
#
# -Dtests=false and -Dconformance=false. BOTH DEFAULT TRUE. Build-time only, but
# nothing here runs them.
#
# -Dintrospection=enabled. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS 'auto'. gobject-introspection is
# packaged, so auto would find it and enable introspection -- the right outcome
# reached by accident, and one that would silently reverse on any image where
# gobject-introspection happened to be absent. Named so the recipe determines it.
# Enabled rather than disabled because json-glib is a GNOME library that
# consumers expect to have GIR data, and gtk4 in this distribution is already
# built with introspection on; a JSON-GLib without it would be an odd exception
# that fails obscurely later rather than here.
#
# -Ddocumentation=disabled and -Dgtk_doc=disabled. BOTH DEFAULT 'auto' and both
# need gi-docgen, which is NOT packaged. Left at auto they would silently
# resolve to off -- the right outcome for the wrong reason, and indistinguishable
# from nobody having looked. gtk_doc is marked deprecated in favour of
# documentation but is still present, so both are named.
#
# -Dnls=enabled. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS 'auto'. gettext is packaged, so this is the
# outcome auto would reach; named for the same reason as introspection.
#
# -Dman=false is already the default (it needs xsltproc, which is not packaged).
# Named so the absence is a decision rather than a gap.
MESON_ARGS="-Dintrospection=enabled -Dnls=enabled \
-Ddocumentation=disabled -Dgtk_doc=disabled -Dman=false \
-Dtests=false -Dconformance=false -Dinstalled_tests=false"
